            <ArticleTitle>[Pancreatic head resection (Frey technique) and Wirsungo-jejunal anastomosis in the treatment of chronic pancreatitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>647-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report herein a modification of the standard wirsungojejunostomy in patients with chronic pancreatitis, which includes concomitant duodenum-preserving resection of the head of the pancreas as described by Frey. This technique is safe and seems to provide more effective long-term pain relief than standard wirsungo-jejunal anastomosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
